The examples follow the revision in the [ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/quickstart')).

# [Tagged dot product]($heading.id('tagged-dot-product'))

Follow a **2 × 3 weight matrix** and a three-element input through `forward`.
The `.feature` tag identifies the columns in the weights and the only axis
in the input.

```=html
<div class="contraction-explorer" data-contraction-explorer>
  <div class="contraction-steps" role="group" aria-label="Dot product steps" hidden data-pagefind-ignore>
    <button type="button" data-select-stage="inspect" aria-pressed="true">Inspect axes</button>
    <button type="button" data-select-stage="multiply" aria-pressed="false">Multiply</button>
    <button type="button" data-select-stage="sum" aria-pressed="false">Sum rows</button>
  </div>
  <div class="contraction-workspace">
    <figure>
      <figcaption><strong>Weights</strong><code>f32[2, 3]</code></figcaption>
      <table class="contraction-grid" aria-label="Weight matrix with two output rows, three feature columns, and an aligned input vector">
        <colgroup><col class="contraction-row-column"></colgroup>
        <colgroup span="3"></colgroup>
        <colgroup><col class="contraction-result-column"></colgroup>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3" data-select-axis="feature"><code>.feature</code></th>
            <th scope="col" rowspan="2" class="contraction-result-label">Result</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" data-select-axis="output"><code>.output</code></th>
            <th scope="col">0</th>
            <th scope="col">1</th>
            <th scope="col">2</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">0</th><td data-weight>1</td><td data-weight>2</td><td data-weight>3</td><td data-result>13</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-weight>4</td><td data-weight>5</td><td data-weight>6</td><td data-result>31</td></tr>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr><th scope="row">Input</th><td data-input>2</td><td data-input>1</td><td data-input>3</td><td></td></tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
      <div role="status">
        <p class="contraction-status">Sum three feature products per row. Result <code>f32[2]</code> · <code>.output</code> · Rank 1</p>
        <p class="contraction-rule" data-matching-rule>Both <code>.feature</code> axes must have the same size.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <div class="command-shell contraction-code">
      <span class="command-language icon-code">Zig · forward</span>
      <pre><code data-copy-label="Copy tagged dot product in Zig"><span class="token keyword">const</span> zml = <span class="token builtin">@import</span>(<span class="token string">"zml"</span>);

<span class="token keyword">pub fn</span> forward(weights: zml.Tensor, input: zml.Tensor) zml.Tensor {
<span data-line="weights">    <span class="token keyword">const</span> tagged_weights = weights.<span class="token function">withTags</span>(.{ <span class="token attr-name">.output</span>, <span class="token attr-name">.feature</span> });</span>
<span data-line="input">    <span class="token keyword">const</span> tagged_input = input.<span class="token function">withTags</span>(.{<span class="token attr-name">.feature</span>});</span>
<span data-line="dot">    <span class="token keyword">return</span> tagged_weights.<span class="token function">dot</span>(tagged_input, <span class="token attr-name">.feature</span>);</span>
}
</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<details class="contraction-batch-note">
  <summary>Batched inputs</summary>
  <p>In <code>dot</code>, other axes with matching tags are paired as batch axes.</p>
</details>
```

