# [Tensors]($heading.id('tensors'))

`zml.Tensor` describes a symbolic value. `zml.Buffer` holds its data at runtime.

[]($section.attrs('contraction-definition'))

# [Shapes]($heading.id('shapes'))

A shape records the element type and ordered axis sizes. Rank counts the axes.

```=html
<div class="contraction-shape-examples">
  <span><code>f32[]</code> Scalar · rank 0</span>
  <span><code>f32[1]</code> One-element vector · rank 1</span>
</div>
```

[Shape API →]($link.page('zml/api/shape').ref('shape'))

[]($section.attrs('contraction-definition'))

# [Dimension tags]($heading.id('dimension-tags'))

`withTags` names axes in their existing order. `axis(tag)` returns the index
and `dim(tag)` returns the size.
